### C. Zero-Breaking-Changes Forwarding Shims
To guarantee that existing code (e.g. `navigate.py`, visualization scripts, and external callers) never breaks:
- [backend/models/drainage.py](file:///c:/Users/aksha/urbanFlood/backend/models/drainage.py) -> re-exports from `backend.app.models.drainage`
- [backend/models/routing.py](file:///c:/Users/aksha/urbanFlood/backend/models/routing.py) -> re-exports from `backend.app.models.routing`
- [backend/models/location.py](file:///c:/Users/aksha/urbanFlood/backend/models/location.py) -> re-exports from `backend.app.models.location`
- [backend/api/drainage.py](file:///c:/Users/aksha/urbanFlood/backend/api/drainage.py) -> re-exports from `backend.app.api.drainage`
- [backend/api/roads.py](file:///c:/Users/aksha/urbanFlood/backend/api/roads.py) -> re-exports from `backend.app.api.roads`
- [backend/api/route.py](file:///c:/Users/aksha/urbanFlood/backend/api/route.py) -> re-exports from `backend.app.api.route`
- [backend/main.py](file:///c:/Users/aksha/urbanFlood/backend/main.py) -> forwards directly to `backend.app.main:app`

### D. Single Unified FastAPI Application
[backend/app/main.py](file:///c:/Users/aksha/urbanFlood/backend/app/main.py) now mounts **all 7 routers**:
1. `/api/flood-forecast` (Pair B Overland Simulation & Depth Grids)
2. `/api/simulate` (On-Demand Scenario Execution)
3. `/api/rainfall` (Doppler Radar & Marshall-Palmer Z-R Frames)
4. `/api/drainage` (Pair A Pipe Capacity, Inlets & Surcharge)
5. `/api/roads` (Pair C Road Network & Inundation Hotspots)
6. `/api/route` (Flood-Resilient A* Evacuation Routing)
7. `/ws/flood-updates` (Real-Time Live Streaming WebSocket)

